# iHub Apps process settings
#
# Only read by the single-executable (SEA) distribution: `build-sea.cjs` copies
# this file next to the binary and the launcher loads it with dotenv. It is NOT
# read by `npm start`, `npm run dev` or Docker — those use a plain `.env` file
# or real environment variables.
#
# It holds the few settings the process needs before the platform
# configuration is loaded. Everything else is configured in the admin UI
# (stored in `contents/config/`):
#
#   - LLM provider and model API keys: Admin → Providers / Admin → Models
#     (encrypted at rest). Do not put keys in this file.
#   - Web search keys (Brave, Staan): Admin → Providers
#   - Proxy: Admin → Security → Outbound Proxy (`proxy` in platform.json)
#   - Timeouts, authentication, CORS, ...: `contents/config/platform.json`
#
# New settings will not be added here.

# Server
PORT=3001                # Port the server listens on
HOST=0.0.0.0             # 0.0.0.0 accepts connections from any IP, 127.0.0.1 is local only
WORKERS=1                # Worker processes (more than 1 enables clustering)

# HTTPS (optional)
#SSL_KEY=/path/to/your/key.pem     # Private key
#SSL_CERT=/path/to/your/cert.pem   # Certificate
#SSL_CA=/path/to/your/ca.pem       # CA certificate (optional)

# Custom CA / PKI (optional)
#NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/path/company-ca.pem

# Location of the contents directory (optional, default: contents)
#CONTENTS_DIR=contents
